6. Develop an Android application demonstrating communication between Activity and Fragment. 
 
Theory 
An Activity acts as the main entry point of an Android application, while a Fragment represents a reusable portion 
of the user interface. 
Communication between an Activity and a Fragment can occur in two ways: 
1. Activity → Fragment: Data is passed using a Bundle.  
2. Fragment → Activity: Data is sent back using an interface callback implemented by the Activity.  
This approach promotes modular, reusable, and maintainable Android applications. 
